  "body": "I think the desired behavior is that it's unspecified, because in practice implementations do not have a consistent order, and I recall past discussions were that some of them aren't willing to change.  This should be specified explicitly, because it could be argued that the order should obviously match the DOM order unless specified otherwise.  Alternatively, if implementations are willing to converge, we could specify that they match some specified order (e.g., DOM order).\n",
